el":"Load and Validate Model","html_id":"load-and-validate-model","implicit":true,"key":"SUmHLP7riH"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":75,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"This code uses the ","position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"key":"FTfc1tbWHQ"},{"type":"link","url":"https://github.com/NREL/BuildingMOTIF","position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"BuildingMOTIF","position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"key":"q1bVFk4yfZ"}],"urlSource":"https://github.com/NREL/BuildingMOTIF","error":true,"key":"Unwfh2K07r"},{"type":"text","value":" library to load the 223P ontology and the model file into a temporary in-memory instance.\nIt then validates the model against the ontology. If the model is invalid, it will print the validation report.","position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"key":"PH1n8VB64N"}],"key":"cSx9xrXIUc"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":77,"column":1},"end":{"line":78,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"BuildingMOTIF resolves the ontology’s dependencies with ","position":{"start":{"line":77,"column":1},"end":{"line":77,"column":1}},"key":"JLHcZ34G3g"},{"type":"link","url":"https://ontoenv.gtf.fyi","position":{"start":{"line":77,"column":1},"end":{"line":77,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"OntoEnv","position":{"start":{"line":77,"column":1},"end":{"line":77,"column":1}},"key":"I7x5T6jC3U"}],"urlSource":"https://ontoenv.gtf.fyi","key":"U4p6wgFkBI"},{"type":"text","value":" and validates with\n","position":{"start":{"line":77,"column":1},"end":{"line":77,"column":1}},"key":"CivyUek7ne"},{"type":"link","url":"https://shifty.gtf.fyi","position":{"start":{"line":77,"column":1},"end":{"line":77,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"shifty","position":{"start":{"line":77,"column":1},"end":{"line":77,"column":1}},"key":"Uf8emNEO6j"}],"urlSource":"https://shifty.gtf.fyi","key":"RsXLFcdCKp"},{"type":"text","value":", both of which are self-contained Rust extensions, so there is nothing else to install and no Java is required.","position":{"start":{"line":77,"column":1},"end":{"line":77,"column":1}},"key":"XQQCZB3zNn"}],"key":"qmNQoXWgQL"},{"type":"admonition","kind":"note","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"BuildingMOTIF installation","position":{"start":{"line":80,"column":1},"end":{"line":80,"column":1}},"key":"fLn71154RO"}],"key":"xdUeRJ65Lw"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":82,"column":1},"end":{"line":82,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"To install the ","position":{"start":{"line":82,"column":1},"end":{"line":82,"column":1}},"key":"ykOI5uTiuL"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"buildingmotif","position":{"start":{"line":82,"column":1},"end":{"line":82,"column":1}},"key":"WrxwnP2fUL"},{"type":"text","value":" library, you can use the following command:","position":{"start":{"line":82,"column":1},"end":{"line":82,"column":1}},"key":"cSZcI7LzSg"}],"key":"Je84yP5cM8"},{"type":"code","lang":"shell","value":"pip install 'buildingmotif @ git+https://github.com/NREL/buildingmotif.git@gtf-buildingmotif'","position":{"start":{"line":84,"column":1},"end":{"line":86,"column":1}},"key":"wjpBSGBhWh"}],"class":"dropdown","key":"JdcaNqecx2"}],"key":"hO6PB34aeh"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"from buildingmotif import BuildingMOTIF\nfrom buildingmotif.dataclasses import Library, Model\nimport logging\n\n# Create a BuildingMOTIF object. This validates with the \"pyshifty\" SHACL\n# engine by default, so there is nothing else to install and no Java required.\nbm = BuildingMOTIF('sqlite://', log_level=logging.ERROR)\n\n# load 223P library. We will load a recent copy from the models.open223.info\n# git repository; later, we will load this from the location of the actual standard.\n# BuildingMOTIF uses OntoEnv to fetch the ontologies 223P depends on (QUDT, SHACL, ...).\ns223 = Library.from_ontology(\"https://open223.info/223p.ttl\", infer_templates=False, run_shacl_inference=False)\n\n# load the model into the BuildingMOTIF instance\nmodel = Model.from_file(\"https://models.open223.info/design-patterns.ttl\")\n\n# a model's manifest lists the libraries it should conform to\nmodel.manifest.add(s223)\n\n# validate the model against its manifest\nctx = model.validate()\n\n# print the validation result\nprint(f\"Model is valid: {ctx.valid}\")\n\n# if the model is invalid, print the validation report\nif not ctx.valid:\n    print(ctx.report_string[:1000]) # first 1000 characters of the report\n\n# BuildingMOTIF can also interpret the report to provide recommendations on fixes\nfor focus_node, diffs in ctx.get_reasons_with_severity(\"Violation\").items():\n    if len(diffs) == 0:\n        continue\n    print(focus_node)\n    for diff in diffs:\n        print(\"  - \" + diff.reason())","key":"PkRNCJt8k1"},{"type":"outputs","id":"Ixj7eoKPDDpVUs5sCY404","children":[{"type":"output","children":[],"jupyter_data":{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":"Model is valid: False\nValidation Report\nConforms: False\n\nViolation result in http://data.ashrae.org/standard223#EnumerableProperty (<http://data.ashrae.org/standard223/1.0/data/patterns-scenario2#LuminaireCommand>):\n  Path: <http://data.ashrae.org/standard223#hasEnumerationKind>\n  Severity: Violation\n  Value: <http://data.ashrae.org/standard223#EnumerationKind-OnOff>\n  Message: must be an instance of <http://data.ashrae.org/standard223#EnumerationKind>\n\nViolation result in http://data.ashrae.org/standard223#ConnectionPoint (<http://data.ashrae.org/standard223/1.0/data/patterns-scenario3#BreakerOutletConnectionPoint_1>):\n  Path: <http://data.ashrae.org/standard223#isConnectionPointOf>\n  Severity: Violation\n  Value: <http://data.as